    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in Sjögren:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " dry mouth: cevimeline 30 mg PO 3 times a day (or pilocarpine 5 mg) can stimulate saliva; avoid w bronchospasm or closed-angle glaucoma."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) dose, dry mouth in Sjögren's syndrome:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 30 mg taken three times a day; insufficient safety information to support doses greater than 30 mg tid."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " uncontrolled asthma, known hypersensitivity to cevimeline, and when miosis is undesirable, e.g., acute iritis and narrow-angle (angle-closure) glaucoma."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) cardiovascular:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Can potentially alter cardiac conduction and/or HR; pts w significant cardiovascular dz may be unable to compensate for transient changes in hemodynamics or rhythm; use w caution and under close medical supervision in pts w Hx of cardiovascular dz evidenced by angina pectoris or myocardial infarction."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) pulmonary:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Can potentially ↑ airway resistance, bronchial smooth muscle tone, and bronchial secretions; administer w caution and w close medical supervision to pts w controlled asthma, chronic bronchitis, or chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) ocular:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Ophthalmic formulations of muscarinic agonists reported to cause visual blurring which may result in ↓ visual acuity, especially at night and in pts w central lens changes, and to cause impairment of depth perception; caution advised while driving at night or performing hazardous activities in reduced lighting."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) CYP2D6/CYP3A3/4 interactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Drugs which inhibit CYP2D6 and CYP3A3/4 also inhibit the metabolism of cevimeline; use w caution in pts known or suspected to be deficient in CYP2D6 activity, as they may be at ↑ risk of adverse events. Use w caution in pts taking beta adrenergic antagonists, because of the possibility of conduction disturbances."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) OD signs:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Toxicity = exaggerated parasympathomimetic effects: headache, visual disturbance, lacrimation, sweating, respiratory distress, gastrointestinal spasm, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, atrioventricular block, tachycardia, bradycardia, hypotension, hypertension, shock, mental confusion, cardiac arrhythmia, and tremors."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) OD management:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Manage as for other muscarinic agonists w general supportive measures; if medically indicated, atropine may be of value as an antidote for emergency use in pts who have had an OD; epinephrine may also be of value in severe cardiovascular depression or bronchoconstriction."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
